{
  "configuration_id": "config_012",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_013: image_only, singleprofile, ViT-L → 22.7% acc), which is an extremely sparse evidence base. The most fundamental uncertainty for a multimodal cellular-profiling study is whether adding the RNA modality provides any signal beyond the image alone. config_012 (multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, aggregation=None, fusion=weighted) matches the baseline on every shared axis—same image encoder (ViT-L), same profile setting (singleprofile), no aggregation—so the only major change is the addition of a pretrained single-cell RNA encoder (scgpt) with a weighted fusion. This gives a clean, near-controlled comparison that isolates the contribution of the RNA modality. If accuracy improves meaningfully over 22.7%, we gain confidence to invest in RNA encoder and fusion choices; if it does not, we learn that the image pathway or the task itself is the bottleneck and can redirect budget toward image-encoder or profile-setting experiments. Under a tight budget, resolving this binary question (does RNA help?) is the highest-information next step before exploring finer-grained design axes."
}

